Was not able to reproduce the crash, but I'm getting long freezes (usually it's recovering in a few minutes, but not always) on 75% load. With the following patch, it loads in 5 sec consistently without freezes, so the aforementioned race condition in the `CommandQueue` is likely the reason.

```diff
diff --git a/core/templates/command_queue_mt.h b/core/templates/command_queue_mt.h
index 5950834804..0110771f15 100644
--- a/core/templates/command_queue_mt.h
+++ b/core/templates/command_queue_mt.h
@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@ class CommandQueueMT {
 	uint32_t sync_awaiters = 0;
 	WorkerThreadPool::TaskID pump_task_id = WorkerThreadPool::INVALID_TASK_ID;
 	uint64_t flush_read_ptr = 0;
+	std::atomic<bool> pending;

 	template <typename T, typename... Args>
 	_FORCE_INLINE_ void create_command(Args &&...p_args) {
@@ -125,6 +126,7 @@ class CommandQueueMT {
 		command_mem.resize(size + alloc_size + sizeof(uint64_t));
 		*(uint64_t *)&command_mem[size] = alloc_size;
 		void *cmd = &command_mem[size + sizeof(uint64_t)];
+		pending.store(true);
 		new (cmd) T(std::forward<Args>(p_args)...);
 	}

@@ -185,6 +187,7 @@ class CommandQueueMT {
 			flush_read_ptr += size;
 		}

+		pending.store(false);
 		command_mem.clear();
 		flush_read_ptr = 0;

@@ -226,7 +229,7 @@ public:
 	}

 	_FORCE_INLINE_ void flush_if_pending() {
-		if (unlikely(command_mem.size() > 0)) {
+		if (unlikely(pending.load())) {
 			_flush();
 		}
```

I was able to reproduce the crash a well (it's hard to reproduce, clear shader cache required, delete `~/Library/Application Support/Godot/app_userdata/Godot Third-Person Shooter Demo/shader_cache` to test), `spirv_cross` seems to be involved, different places, but it's always hitting thread stack guard while trying to allocate string, so it might be thread stack size issue (which is hardcoded to 512KiB for `std::string` and impossible to change):
```
VM Region Info: 0x16d74bff8 is in 0x16d748000-0x16d74c000;  bytes after start: 16376  bytes before end: 7
      REGION TYPE                    START - END         [ VSIZE] PRT/MAX SHRMOD  REGION DETAIL
      Stack                       16d6c0000-16d748000    [  544K] rw-/rwx SM=PRV  thread 13
--->  STACK GUARD                 16d748000-16d74c000    [   16K] ---/rwx SM=NUL  stack guard for thread 14
      Stack                       16d74c000-16d7d4000    [  544K] rw-/rwx SM=PRV  thread 14
```

`CommandQueue` race condition, likely a separate issue and not related to crash directly.

With threading switched to `pthreads` (macOS/iOS use it under the hood anyway, so it's not a big change) and thread stack size increased to 8MB, it is no longer crashing. But `ResourceLoader` sometimes deadlocking after shader compilation. So this might be 3 issues in one:

- Race condition in `CommandQueue`.
- `spirv_cross` thread running out of stack space.
- Deadlock in `ResourceLoader` (~or it's `std` interlocking not properly working with raw pthread~ *probably no, I made a hacky version that's hijacking `std::thread` creation and deadlock is still there*).

Here's patch for first two for testing:
```diff
diff --git a/core/os/thread.h b/core/os/thread.h
index 472998673a..e7454cb5b2 100644
--- a/core/os/thread.h
+++ b/core/os/thread.h
@@ -56,7 +56,24 @@
 #include "thirdparty/mingw-std-threads/mingw.thread.h"
 #define THREADING_NAMESPACE mingw_stdthread
 #else
+#if defined(MACOS_ENABLED) || defined(IOS_ENABLED)
+#include <__threading_support>
+_LIBCPP_BEGIN_NAMESPACE_STD
+static inline int __libcpp_thread_create_with_stack(__libcpp_thread_t *thread_id, void *(*thread_func)(void *arg), void *arg) {
+	pthread_attr_t attr;
+	pthread_attr_init(&attr);
+	pthread_attr_setstacksize(&attr, 8 * 1024 * 1024);
+	int ret = pthread_create(thread_id, &attr, thread_func, arg);
+	pthread_attr_destroy(&attr);
+	return ret;
+}
+_LIBCPP_END_NAMESPACE_STD
+#define __libcpp_thread_create __libcpp_thread_create_with_stack
 #include <thread>
+#undef __libcpp_thread_create
+#else
+#include <thread>
+#endif
 #define THREADING_NAMESPACE std
 #endif

diff --git a/core/templates/command_queue_mt.h b/core/templates/command_queue_mt.h
index 5950834804..576b2ff892 100644
--- a/core/templates/command_queue_mt.h
+++ b/core/templates/command_queue_mt.h
@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@ class CommandQueueMT {
 	uint32_t sync_awaiters = 0;
 	WorkerThreadPool::TaskID pump_task_id = WorkerThreadPool::INVALID_TASK_ID;
 	uint64_t flush_read_ptr = 0;
+	std::atomic<bool> pending;

 	template <typename T, typename... Args>
 	_FORCE_INLINE_ void create_command(Args &&...p_args) {
@@ -126,6 +127,7 @@ class CommandQueueMT {
 		*(uint64_t *)&command_mem[size] = alloc_size;
 		void *cmd = &command_mem[size + sizeof(uint64_t)];
 		new (cmd) T(std::forward<Args>(p_args)...);
+		pending.store(true);
 	}

 	template <typename T, bool NeedsSync, typename... Args>
@@ -186,6 +188,7 @@ class CommandQueueMT {
 		}

 		command_mem.clear();
+		pending.store(false);
 		flush_read_ptr = 0;

 		_prevent_sync_wraparound();
@@ -226,7 +229,7 @@ public:
 	}

 	_FORCE_INLINE_ void flush_if_pending() {
-		if (unlikely(command_mem.size() > 0)) {
+		if (unlikely(pending.load())) {
 			_flush();
 		}
 	}

```

